## Runtime contract
The platform builds the app, starts it with `python app.py` and checks the following automatically.
- `GET {{ contract.health_path }}` returns HTTP 200 with a JSON body.
- All API routes live under `/api/`, and the server listens on `0.0.0.0:8000`.
- The built frontend is copied to `./static`: serve its files by path, and `index.html` for `/` and for every other non-API path (client-side routes).
- Data lives in SQLite at `/app/data/app.db`; the app starts from an empty `data/` directory, so it creates its schema (and any seed data) at startup.
